  "script": "Beavers live in freshwater ecosystems such as rivers, streams, lakes and ponds across various landscapes. In Europe, beavers were reduced to fragmented populations with combined population numbers being estimated. These historical reductions affected populations within regions like the Rhône of France and the Elbe. Similar fragmented groups survived near southern Norway and the Neman river and Dnieper Basin. Additional survivors persisted along the Voronezh river in Russia within similar freshwater habitats. The keystone species concept became popular in conservation and was deployed in various contexts. This conservation framework was mobilized to engender support where human activities had damaged ecosystems. Stream restoration or river restoration activities aim to improve the environmental health of a system.",
